refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;

 stringfalsesession_module_name
 stringnullmodule&null;


 session_module_name gets or sets the name of the current
 session module, which is also known as
 session.save_handler.

&reftitle.parameters;
module
If module is specified and not &null;, that module will be used instead. session_module_name needs to be called before session_start for that purpose. Passing "user" to this parameter is forbidden. Instead session_set_save_handler has to be called to set a user defined session handler.

&reftitle.returnvalues;
Returns the name of the current session module, &return.falseforfailure;. When module is specified, the name of the module that was in use before the call is returned. An empty string is returned if session.save_handler was set to a module that does not exist. "user" is returned once session_set_save_handler has been called.
&false; is returned, and an E_WARNING is raised, if module is specified and a session is active, headers have already been sent, or no module with that name exists.
